Error [E3412]: `core.net.tcp_connect()` is not available at comptime
  --> tests/ui/impure_net_stub.jet:6:29
    |
  6 |         comptime conn = net.tcp_connect("build.example.com:443")
    |                             ^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: only `core.net.fetch(url, sha256:)` is supported at compile time
 Fix: use `core.net.fetch(url, sha256: "<hash>")` for content-hash-pinned downloads

Error [E0915]: `TcpStream ? NetError` has no `Display` implementation
  --> tests/ui/impure_net_stub.jet:7:28
    |
  7 |         print("connected: {conn}")
    |                            ^^^^
 Why: bare `{value}` interpolation calls `Display` — there is no default for user types
 Fix: add `impl TcpStream ? NetError.Display { fn display(self) -> String { … } }`, or use `{value@Debug}` for debug output
